    "content": "Somalia's Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Ahmed Moallim Fiqi, attended the 49th Ordinary Session of the African Union (AU) Executive Council, which opened in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia, on July 18, 2025. The session is themed 'Securing Sustainable Access to Water,' highlighting the AU's priority on water security and management across Africa.\n\nThe minister joined other foreign ministers and senior officials from AU member states to discuss the continent's pressing water challenges, including scarcity, climate change impacts, and transboundary water governance. The three-day meeting aims to develop collective strategies to ensure reliable water supplies for communities, agriculture, and industries.\n\nSomalia's active participation underscores its commitment to regional cooperation on shared resources. As a country grappling with recurrent droughts and water insecurity, the outcomes of this session are particularly relevant for Somali communities, both at home and abroad. The diaspora, often engaged in relief efforts, stands to benefit from coordinated AU policies that could improve water infrastructure and crisis response.\n\nThe Executive Council will also review reports from AU specialized committees and consider recommendations for the upcoming Assembly of Heads of State and Government. This session builds on the AU's 2025 theme of water security, aiming to translate commitments into actionable projects.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/wasiirka-arrimaha-dibadda-oo-ka-qeybgalay-kalfadhiga-49-aad-ee-golaha-fulinta-midowga-afrika/424255/",
