    "content": "The Danab commando forces, a Somali special operations unit active in Puntland, released a press statement on Thursday alerting the public to the potential outbreak of fighting in the region. The statement highlighted that they had received intelligence indicating possible attacks against Puntland Security Force (PSF) personnel. Danab emphasized that the ongoing political dispute in Puntland is internal in nature and does not stem from any external threat to the administration.\n\nThe commandos directed their criticism at Puntland President Said Abdullahi Deni, holding him responsible for heightening tensions and creating conditions that could lead to internecine conflict. They asserted that the president's actions are exacerbating the political crisis, which has already caused divisions within the region.\n\nThis warning comes amid a prolonged political standoff in Puntland, where President Deni has been locked in a power struggle with opposition figures and federal authorities. The region has seen sporadic violence in recent months, raising concerns about stability in an area that has been a key partner in the fight against al-Shabaab.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development is significant because Puntland's stability directly affects the security and economic ties that connect them to their homeland. Many diaspora families have relatives in Puntland, and any escalation of conflict could disrupt remittance flows and travel. Additionally, political instability in Puntland undermines broader Somali federalism efforts, which the diaspora has long supported.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/29/ciidanka-kumaandooska-danab-oo-ka-digay-dagaal-ka-dhaca-puntland-eedeynna-u-jeediyay-madaxweyne-siciid-deni/",
