    "summary": "Somalia's delegation, led by Foreign Minister Abdusalam Abdi Ali, attends the 49th African Union Executive Council session in Addis Ababa. The session focuses on sustainable water access and climate resilience.",
    "content": "Somalia is participating in the 49th ordinary session of the African Union Executive Council, convening in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia. The delegation is headed by Foreign Minister Abdusalam Abdi Ali (Dhaay), representing the Federal Government of Somalia.\n\nThe session prioritizes the theme \"Ensuring Sustainable Access to Water,\" prompting member states to collaborate on addressing water-related challenges and climate change impacts. Discussions are centered on developing joint strategies to mitigate water scarcity and adapt to shifting weather patterns.\n\nSomalia’s involvement underscores its reliance on transboundary water resources and vulnerability to droughts, which affect millions in the region. The country advocates for shared solutions that account for the needs of drought-prone nations.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, engagement in AU policy-making signals continued diplomatic efforts toward stability and resource security. These initiatives directly affect family members back home who face water shortages.\n\nSomali officials aim to leverage the forum to highlight national priorities and secure support for water infrastructure projects. The session reflects broader AU goals of achieving water security across the continent.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/28/soomaaliya-oo-ka-qaybgalaysa-kalfadhiga-49-aad-ee-golaha-fulinta-midowga-afrika/",
